From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: msm8998: do not power-collapse the firmware

Every path back from a firmware power collapse on msm8998 is broken:

 - TZ's own restore (scm_set_remote_state resume) returns success and
   hands back an ARM9 that is out of WFI but services nothing -- not
   even a manually fired CPU_IC_SOFTINT, measured via /dev/mem.
 - A full reboot at resume (shutdown, fresh queues, PAS re-auth, boot,
   SYS_INIT) boots to CTRL_INIT-done and then SYS_INIT gets silence.
 - Even a complete driver unbind/rebind -- the virgin cold-probe path --
   fails with -EINVAL once the firmware has been shut down that boot.

Only the very first bring-up per boot works, and it works perfectly:
bit-exact decode, sequential sessions, stable for as long as the core
is not collapsed. Whatever handshake the vendor's power-collapse
contract contains beyond rates, IMEM, thresholds, retention and call
order, five instrumented bisect arms did not find it.

So stop collapsing: forbid runtime PM on the venus core. The device
powers up at first use and stays up while the driver is bound.

ponytail: this trades idle power (VIDEO_TOP GDSC + core clocks stay on
once venus is used) for a firmware that always works. The ceiling is a
daily-driver battery cost; the upgrade path is the vendor's PC contract,
taken to linux-media with the bisect evidence.

This replaces the reboot-on-resume attempt, which is reverted here.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 42 ++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 7eec533c5d4b..9eba36ec67b0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -562,6 +562,13 @@ static int venus_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_of_depopulate;
 
+	/*
+	 * msm8998: the firmware does not survive any power collapse (see
+	 * venus_runtime_resume); keep the core powered while bound.
+	 */
+	if (IS_V3(core))
+		pm_runtime_forbid(dev);
+
 	ret = pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
@@ -725,41 +732,6 @@ static __maybe_unused int venus_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (venus_stop_before(6))
 		return 0;
 
-	/*
-	 * msm8998's TZ restore hands back a wedged firmware: resume is
-	 * accepted, the CTRL_INIT poll passes, and the ARM9 then ignores
-	 * even a manually fired CPU_IC_SOFTINT. When the firmware was up
-	 * before this collapse, reboot it the way sys_error recovery does
-	 * instead of trusting the restore. The fw is dead, so there is no
-	 * HFI goodbye to say -- drop the state and start over.
-	 */
-	if (IS_V3(core) && core->state == CORE_INIT) {
-		mutex_lock(&core->lock);
-		core->state = CORE_UNINIT;
-		venus_shutdown(core);
-		mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
-
-		hfi_reinit(core);
-
-		ret = venus_boot(core);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
-
-		ret = hfi_core_resume(core, true);
-		if (ret)
-			goto err_shutdown;
-
-		ret = hfi_core_init(core);
-		if (ret)
-			goto err_shutdown;
-
-		return 0;
-
-err_shutdown:
-		venus_shutdown(core);
-		return ret;
-	}
-
 	return hfi_core_resume(core, false);
 }
 
